4 Son of your Father's eternal love,
Take to yourself your mighty power;
Let all earth's sons your mercy know,
Let all adore your bleeding grace.
Display the triumphs of your love;
In every heart reign you alone;
Till all your foes confess your sway,
And glory ends what grace began.

8 Giver and Lord of life, whose power
And guardian care are free to all;
To you, in fierce temptation's hour,
From sin and Satan let us flee.
Yours, Lord, we are, and ours you are;
In us be all your goodness shown;
Renew, enlarge, and fill our heart
With peace, and joy, and heaven, and God.
